1
00:02:31,069 --> 00:02:41,069
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,069 --> 00:02:45,069
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,069 --> 00:02:52,069
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,069 --> 00:02:58,069
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,069 --> 00:03:09,069
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,069 --> 00:03:13,069
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:19,069 --> 00:03:27,069
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:28,069 --> 00:03:35,069
The Fishman Pirates, led by Hordy Jones and assisted by Vander Decken, plot to overthrow King Neptune.

9
00:03:35,069 --> 00:03:43,069
It's not long before the Straw Hats get pulled into the conflict and find themselves in the midst of an all-out war.

10
00:03:43,069 --> 00:03:47,069
If you want to take my life, then I am powerless to stop you!

11
00:03:47,069 --> 00:03:50,069
But no one else should have to suffer!

12
00:03:50,069 --> 00:03:52,069
I won't let you harm this kingdom!

13
00:03:52,069 --> 00:03:54,069
I will protect it with my life!

14
00:03:54,069 --> 00:03:58,069
So come get me, you monster!

15
00:03:58,069 --> 00:04:23,069
Damn it, weepy Hoshi! I told you to stay where I can protect you!

16
00:04:23,069 --> 00:04:42,069
I'll show you what happens to traitors, Vander Decken. But I do admit I like this idea of yours.

17
00:04:42,069 --> 00:04:56,069
I can't believe I'm letting you save the girl! You better not let us down! Don't hold anything back, Luffy!

18
00:05:00,069 --> 00:05:01,069
Here I go!

19
00:05:01,069 --> 00:05:07,069
Hurry up, Luffy! Shira Hoshi's life in jeopardy!

20
00:05:31,069 --> 00:05:36,069
Whoa! What's it doing?

21
00:05:41,069 --> 00:05:46,069
It's leaving! Look! And Noah's not headed toward the island anymore!

22
00:05:46,069 --> 00:05:50,069
The Princess is leading it away from us! It won't crash into us after all!

23
00:05:50,069 --> 00:05:52,069
Don't let it hit you!

24
00:05:52,069 --> 00:05:54,069
Swim faster!

25
00:05:54,069 --> 00:06:06,069
Where do you think you're going? You know you can't run away, don't you? There is no escape!

26
00:06:11,069 --> 00:06:16,069
If I'm going to steer the Noah clear of the bubble, then I have to swim as far out to sea as I can!

27
00:06:24,069 --> 00:06:27,069
The bubble will surely break if it takes any more damage!

28
00:06:29,069 --> 00:06:31,069
But the main entrance is too far away!

29
00:06:33,069 --> 00:06:38,069
No, wait! I believe Luffy and his friends were the last ones to leave the Ryugu Palace!

30
00:06:40,069 --> 00:06:43,069
If that's the case, perhaps the gateway is still open!

31
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:53,069
Oh no! Isn't there some way to help instead of just standing here?!

32
00:06:53,069 --> 00:06:55,069
What does Vander Decken have to gain from this anyway?!

33
00:06:55,069 --> 00:06:57,069
Leave our princess alone, you monster!

34
00:06:58,069 --> 00:07:01,069
It's not Shira Hoshi's fault! She doesn't deserve to die for this!

35
00:07:02,069 --> 00:07:04,069
Horny's climbing out of the ship too?!

36
00:07:04,069 --> 00:07:07,069
That can't be good! What if he attacks her again?!

37
00:07:07,069 --> 00:07:10,069
There's no one to protect her! She can't fight him!

38
00:07:10,069 --> 00:07:14,069
Decken, you filthy traitor! Have you lost your damned mind?!

39
00:07:15,069 --> 00:07:19,069
This is far from over! I can make use of that madman!

40
00:07:20,069 --> 00:07:22,069
Keep your wits about you, Luffy!

41
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:28,069
Fishmen are far stronger than humans in the water! Do not forget that!

42
00:07:29,069 --> 00:07:30,069
Uh-huh!

43
00:07:31,069 --> 00:07:35,069
I can't throw Luffy too hard or he'll break through the bubble and go flying out to sea!

44
00:07:35,069 --> 00:07:37,069
So I'm gonna have to do it extra carefully!

45
00:07:38,069 --> 00:07:40,069
With exactly the right amount of force!

46
00:07:40,069 --> 00:07:41,069
Now, Sanji!

47
00:07:41,069 --> 00:07:44,069
Arme de lair assault!

48
00:07:46,069 --> 00:07:47,069
Come shoot!

49
00:07:47,069 --> 00:07:49,069
Arme de lair assault!

50
00:08:06,069 --> 00:08:08,069
This thing's pretty big!

51
00:08:10,069 --> 00:08:12,069
I guess I'm between the bubbles now?

52
00:08:12,069 --> 00:08:18,229
Wait, Horty's still under the bubble.

53
00:08:25,909 --> 00:08:32,449
We can't stop this thing, but if we can slow it down, even just a little, maybe she can get away!

54
00:08:33,669 --> 00:08:36,829
Come on! Don't let it catch her!

55
00:08:37,489 --> 00:08:41,109
Hurry, Princess! We'll try to slow it down. You get somewhere safe!

56
00:08:42,069 --> 00:08:47,889
Damn it! It's too heavy!

57
00:08:48,509 --> 00:08:51,389
Are they crazy? My people!

58
00:08:52,269 --> 00:08:58,069
Who came up with that plan? No matter how hard they pull, that ship will never move an inch.

59
00:08:58,429 --> 00:09:00,329
Why don't I just put you out of your misery?

60
00:09:01,009 --> 00:09:02,809
Come on! Back off!

61
00:09:03,069 --> 00:09:04,209
I can't lose!

62
00:09:06,269 --> 00:09:10,949
Aren't you worthless scum? You're the reason humans look down on our entire race.

63
00:09:10,949 --> 00:09:14,429
My kingdom has no place for sentimental weaklings like you!

64
00:09:19,109 --> 00:09:24,489
If your pride as fishmen means nothing to you, then your pathetic lives mean nothing to me!

65
00:09:24,489 --> 00:09:34,349
You soiled the name of our proud race. This is the fate you deserve.

66
00:09:34,349 --> 00:09:46,349
Damn it, Horty!

67
00:09:46,349 --> 00:09:51,349
We're so hurry, your majesty! Just swim away! You're hurrying me!

68
00:09:51,349 --> 00:09:56,229
I mustn't stop now!

69
00:09:59,509 --> 00:10:03,229
I was right! The entrance to the palace is still open!

70
00:10:03,229 --> 00:10:08,189
Just hang in there, buddy! Horty! I'll cut you out!

71
00:10:12,189 --> 00:10:13,769
She made it up to the gate!

72
00:10:15,389 --> 00:10:16,889
She's swimming out to sea!

73
00:10:19,389 --> 00:10:20,989
The Noah's still on her tail!

74
00:10:21,109 --> 00:10:22,429
You can do it, Princess!

75
00:10:22,429 --> 00:10:23,389
PJ Sumpets!

76
00:10:28,989 --> 00:10:30,109
It's going up!

77
00:10:41,189 --> 00:10:41,689
Whoa!

78
00:10:43,009 --> 00:10:45,049
I can't steer this thing!

79
00:10:48,269 --> 00:10:50,589
goat six

80
00:10:50,589 --> 00:10:55,589
Poor, feeble humans. Must be inconvenient.

81
00:10:55,589 --> 00:10:59,589
You all act so high and mighty when you're safe on land.

82
00:10:59,589 --> 00:11:03,589
But here in the water, you're not even a match for the smallest fish man child.

83
00:11:03,589 --> 00:11:07,589
A man is only as strong as he is at his weakest, I'm afraid.

84
00:11:07,589 --> 00:11:13,589
You might be powerful up on the island, but you're in my territory now.

85
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:16,589
Shut up and fight me!

86
00:11:20,589 --> 00:11:30,589
You don't listen very well, do you?

87
00:11:30,589 --> 00:11:33,589
We're not on the ground anymore, kid.

88
00:11:33,589 --> 00:11:38,589
You think you can keep up while you're being tossed around in that bubble?

89
00:11:38,589 --> 00:11:44,589
I hate to break it to you, but if you're worried about Shirahoshi, you're gonna be long dead before that ship hits her.

90
00:11:44,589 --> 00:11:48,589
Speaking of the princess, she did me a favor going out to sea.

91
00:11:48,589 --> 00:11:51,589
You can send her a thank you note from your watery grave!

92
00:11:55,589 --> 00:11:57,589
Shark arrows!

93
00:11:57,589 --> 00:12:13,589
How's that devil fruit power of yours working out by the way? How did you think this would go?

94
00:12:13,589 --> 00:12:18,589
How arrogant to think you had a chance in the sea.

95
00:12:18,589 --> 00:12:21,589
Perhaps you understand at last.

96
00:12:21,589 --> 00:12:26,589
In the bitter end, you humans will finally see that you're unfit to rule this world.

97
00:12:26,589 --> 00:12:28,589
A lesson learned far too late, I'm afraid.

98
00:12:28,589 --> 00:12:32,589
Pathetic. Can't even breathe.

99
00:12:32,589 --> 00:12:39,589
All the fools who enter these waters will pay a high price for their arrogance.

100
00:12:39,589 --> 00:12:44,589
It's far too late now to beg for mercy!

101
00:12:44,589 --> 00:12:47,589
But you're not even capable of that anymore, are you?

102
00:12:47,589 --> 00:12:51,589
Truly such a miserable creature! Now prepare to rot in hell!

103
00:12:51,589 --> 00:12:53,589
Now prepare to rot in hell!

104
00:13:05,589 --> 00:13:06,589
Back for more, are you?

105
00:13:06,589 --> 00:13:16,589
Are you alright? Speak to me, Luffy!

106
00:13:16,589 --> 00:13:19,589
Hey, it's you!

107
00:13:19,589 --> 00:13:22,589
Too bad that kind gesture was in vain.

108
00:13:22,589 --> 00:13:25,589
Because I'm not about to let you get away.

109
00:13:25,589 --> 00:13:27,589
Now say goodbye!

110
00:13:27,589 --> 00:13:29,589
You get away. Now say goodbye!

111
00:13:29,589 --> 00:13:32,589
Tch-he-he-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

112
00:13:32,589 --> 00:13:34,589
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

113
00:13:59,589 --> 00:14:01,589
Paul! Paul!

114
00:14:02,589 --> 00:14:09,589
We can't stop this thing, but if we can slow it down even just a little, maybe she can get away!

115
00:14:09,589 --> 00:14:13,589
Come on! Don't let it catch her!

116
00:14:13,589 --> 00:14:18,589
Hurry, Princess! We'll try to slow it down! You get somewhere safe!

117
00:14:18,589 --> 00:14:25,589
This isn't enough. If I want to save the people of my kingdom, I have to lure the Noah far away from the island!

118
00:14:25,589 --> 00:14:28,589
As far as I possibly can!

119
00:14:28,589 --> 00:14:34,589
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha! I almost forgot to ask Shira Hoshi!

120
00:14:35,589 --> 00:14:36,589
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

121
00:14:36,589 --> 00:14:43,589
How does freedom feel? After ten years, you're no longer protected by the cold stone walls of the hardshell tower!

122
00:14:43,589 --> 00:14:52,589
And now it's time for you to bleed to death, my darling. That is, unless you'd rather be crushed by the massive weight of the Noah!

123
00:14:52,589 --> 00:14:58,589
But one teeny tiny little magic word can spare you this dread fate, and that's yes!

124
00:14:58,589 --> 00:15:01,589
Simply under that one word and your troubles will be over!

125
00:15:01,589 --> 00:15:05,589
I'm deeply sorry, Sir Deccan, but I simply can't do that!

126
00:15:05,589 --> 00:15:07,589
Why must you refuse to marry me?!

127
00:15:07,589 --> 00:15:08,589
Because you're not my type!

128
00:15:08,589 --> 00:15:10,589
Because you're not my type!

129
00:15:10,589 --> 00:15:23,589
I see.

130
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,589
I do hell with you!

131
00:15:25,589 --> 00:15:36,589
Die today! And live for eternity! Deep within my poor, miserable heart! Then you'll be mine! Figuratively at least!

132
00:15:36,589 --> 00:15:45,589
You need to learn how to treat a lady! Or anybody for that matter!

133
00:15:46,589 --> 00:15:51,589
Shira Hoshi is our baby sister! We will never let you lay a hand on her! Not ever!

134
00:15:51,589 --> 00:15:55,589
You came to save me! And Ho is here as well! Thank you!

135
00:15:56,589 --> 00:16:00,589
Oh! Well, hello, brothers-in-law!

136
00:16:00,589 --> 00:16:01,589
We are not your family!

137
00:16:06,589 --> 00:16:10,589
Oh, brothers! Some of our people attempted to save me, but then they were...

138
00:16:11,589 --> 00:16:14,589
Now's not the time for tears, Shira Hoshi!

139
00:16:14,589 --> 00:16:16,589
Oh, please don't get mad at me!

140
00:16:18,589 --> 00:16:19,589
I said don't cry!

141
00:16:19,589 --> 00:16:25,589
Focus, you two! Father told us that we shouldn't let any harm come to the Noah Solatino!

142
00:16:25,589 --> 00:16:30,589
We have to find a way to get it safely back to the sea floor without letting it hit anything along the way!

143
00:16:30,589 --> 00:16:32,589
Look out!

144
00:16:34,589 --> 00:16:38,589
Listen! We need you to mumble your way around the underwater mountains and dritches!

145
00:16:38,589 --> 00:16:40,589
And don't rock the boat, baby!

146
00:16:40,589 --> 00:16:43,589
But there are so many obstacles! Where should I go?

147
00:16:44,589 --> 00:16:48,589
Up there! The path should be a lot clearer that way!

148
00:16:49,589 --> 00:16:51,589
All right, I'll go!

149
00:16:51,589 --> 00:16:54,589
He won't get away from me, Fasola!

150
00:17:02,589 --> 00:17:04,589
You will never escape, my love!

151
00:17:04,589 --> 00:17:08,589
It's as hopeless as you trying to escape the hot pursuit of the Noah!

152
00:17:08,589 --> 00:17:12,589
I'll chase after you as long as I have to, my beautiful bride!

153
00:17:12,589 --> 00:17:22,589
Good thing you showed up! Thanks a lot!

154
00:17:22,589 --> 00:17:25,589
But you got hurt pretty bad back there, are you okay?

155
00:17:25,589 --> 00:17:30,589
My pain means nothing when so many soldiers, citizens, and royal family members were attacked.

156
00:17:31,589 --> 00:17:36,589
Even my sister Shira Hoshi's trying her best to save the Ryugu Kingdom, despite the injury she suffered.

157
00:17:36,589 --> 00:17:42,589
So you see, there simply isn't time for me to sit back and lick my wounds!

158
00:17:43,589 --> 00:17:45,589
Well in that case, can I ask you a favor?

159
00:17:45,589 --> 00:17:48,589
Forgive me, but there's no time for that either!

160
00:17:51,589 --> 00:17:55,589
Furfolk like them are supposed to be the fastest swimmers in the whole world!

161
00:17:55,589 --> 00:17:58,589
But with my new power, I can swim circles around them!

162
00:17:58,589 --> 00:17:59,589
Not again!

163
00:18:01,589 --> 00:18:03,589
Now, Shark Slicer!

164
00:18:06,589 --> 00:18:20,589
Okay, do not let us get hit by that!

165
00:18:21,589 --> 00:18:26,589
Perhaps I'll slice you into nice fillets, then I can feed your flesh to the little fishes!

166
00:18:27,589 --> 00:18:30,589
A prince of the Ryugu Kingdom and a pirate who's worth 400 million!

167
00:18:31,589 --> 00:18:33,589
They're sure to enjoy that meal!

168
00:18:33,589 --> 00:18:35,589
Yeah!

169
00:18:37,589 --> 00:18:40,589
Regardless of where his power comes from, his speed is undeniable!

170
00:18:41,589 --> 00:18:43,589
Hold on tightly, Straw Hat!

171
00:19:03,589 --> 00:19:16,589
He's cutting through stuff just like Zoro! This is crazy!

172
00:19:17,589 --> 00:19:19,589
You should save your admiration for later!

173
00:19:22,589 --> 00:19:27,589
No matter which way you cowards go, you can never outswim the blade of my Shark Slicer!

174
00:19:27,589 --> 00:19:34,589
Hoping you'll lose me in this cloud of dust, are you?

175
00:19:34,589 --> 00:19:35,589
Whoa ha ha!

176
00:19:43,589 --> 00:19:44,589
Huh?

177
00:19:45,589 --> 00:19:46,589
What happened?

178
00:19:46,589 --> 00:19:49,589
Hey, we need to get on top of that ship, quick!

179
00:19:49,589 --> 00:19:50,589
Oh no, no!

180
00:19:50,589 --> 00:19:51,589
What happened?

181
00:19:51,589 --> 00:19:53,589
The Noah!

182
00:19:53,589 --> 00:19:55,589
Baa-ho-ho-ho-ho!

183
00:19:55,589 --> 00:19:58,589
Shira-ho-shi!

184
00:19:58,589 --> 00:20:00,589
What happened?

185
00:20:00,589 --> 00:20:03,589
Hey, we need to get on top of that ship, quick!

186
00:20:03,589 --> 00:20:05,589
Damn you, Deccan.

187
00:20:05,589 --> 00:20:08,589
I assume this is the favor you were going to ask before,

188
00:20:08,589 --> 00:20:10,589
but I failed to see the purpose.

189
00:20:10,589 --> 00:20:12,589
It's something Jinbei told me.

190
00:20:12,589 --> 00:20:15,589
But the ship's in a bubble, so it should be okay!

191
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:16,589
That would make sense.

192
00:20:16,589 --> 00:20:19,589
Deccan is weak to seawater, just like you.

193
00:20:19,589 --> 00:20:22,589
Despite being a fish man, he needs air to move around freely.

194
00:20:22,589 --> 00:20:25,589
It'll be easier for me to fight there,

195
00:20:25,589 --> 00:20:27,589
and I'm about ready to kick the crap out of Hordy

196
00:20:27,589 --> 00:20:29,589
and that weirdo who likes to throw stuff.

197
00:20:29,589 --> 00:20:32,589
Besides, I promised we'd be Hoshi when we left the tower.

198
00:20:32,589 --> 00:20:34,589
I'm supposed to make sure she's safe.

199
00:20:34,589 --> 00:20:37,589
It seems we are of one mind.

200
00:20:37,589 --> 00:20:41,589
And just like our father, your sons will become noble warriors.

201
00:20:41,589 --> 00:20:45,589
With all of our strength,

202
00:20:45,589 --> 00:20:48,589
we will protect Shira Hoshi in body and spirit alike.

203
00:20:48,589 --> 00:20:51,589
I made the same promise.

204
00:20:51,589 --> 00:20:54,589
Yet we allowed ourselves to be bested by a scoundrel

205
00:20:54,589 --> 00:20:56,589
who draws his power from some drug.

206
00:20:56,589 --> 00:20:59,589
It seems I've failed to keep my word to our late mother.

207
00:20:59,589 --> 00:21:02,589
I also regret being suspicious of you at first.

208
00:21:02,589 --> 00:21:05,589
Eh, it's no big deal. Let's head to the deck.

209
00:21:05,589 --> 00:21:07,589
I've got business there too.

210
00:21:07,589 --> 00:21:09,589
What is this?

211
00:21:09,589 --> 00:21:12,589
I can eliminate Straw at any time.

212
00:21:12,589 --> 00:21:14,589
But there's another issue I need to take care of

213
00:21:14,589 --> 00:21:17,589
that simply cannot wait any longer.

214
00:21:17,589 --> 00:21:19,589
What are you waiting for? Come on!

215
00:21:19,589 --> 00:21:21,589
No. We must be cautious.

216
00:21:21,589 --> 00:21:23,589
What do you mean, no?

217
00:21:23,589 --> 00:21:24,589
He's up to something.

218
00:21:24,589 --> 00:21:28,589
More than that, we must be prepared for another encounter underwater.

219
00:21:28,589 --> 00:21:30,589
Clearly our prior approach was inadequate.

220
00:21:30,589 --> 00:21:32,589
So what do we do?

221
00:21:32,589 --> 00:21:34,589
I have an idea.

222
00:21:34,589 --> 00:21:39,589
Please, come on! Higher!

223
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:43,589
You've lived with my markmark curse long enough

224
00:21:43,589 --> 00:21:45,589
to know you can't escape.

225
00:21:45,589 --> 00:21:48,589
And unlike those axes your little tower protected you from,

226
00:21:48,589 --> 00:21:49,589
there's nothing in this wide world

227
00:21:49,589 --> 00:21:53,589
that could stop the Noah from crushing you to itty bitty bits.

228
00:21:53,589 --> 00:21:58,589
Baa-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

229
00:22:01,589 --> 00:22:03,589
Goodness, if it isn't horny, Jones!

230
00:22:03,589 --> 00:22:11,089
Jones say whatever happened to Neptune dead maybe by the way I'm using the

231
00:22:11,089 --> 00:22:17,269
Noah to torture Shirahoshi as we speak a genius idea on my part don't you think

232
00:22:17,269 --> 00:22:28,889
brother it's not bad but I think I've got an even better idea do you now well

233
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:36,289
let's hear it actually it's better if I show you

234
00:22:50,409 --> 00:22:55,289
if you died what would become of this ship

235
00:22:58,889 --> 00:23:01,889
well Deccan

236
00:23:01,889 --> 00:23:14,429
party's unexpected assault on Deccan threatens to destroy all of Fishman Island yet even as

237
